{"content":[{"c":["TEACHER"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Teachers conserved the values and academia of a nation and passed them on to each new generation. In OT times the first teachers were often parents (",{"href":"?bref=Deut.6.7,20-25","r":"Deut.6.7,20-25","rawR":"Deut.6.7,20-25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.6.7,20-25","value":"Deut.6.7,20-25"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 6:7, 20-25"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Deut.11.19-21","r":"Deut.11.19-21","rawR":"Deut.11.19-21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.11.19-21","value":"Deut.11.19-21"}],"t":"ref","v":"11:19-21"},"). Leaders like Moses and Aaron were charged with teaching the people (",{"href":"?bref=Lev.10.11","r":"Lev.10.11","rawR":"Lev.10.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lev.10.11","value":"Lev.10.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lv 10:11"},"), and later the priests and Levites had a teaching function (",{"href":"?bref=Deut.24.8","r":"Deut.24.8","rawR":"Deut.24.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.24.8","value":"Deut.24.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 24:8"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Deut.33.8-10","r":"Deut.33.8-10","rawR":"Deut.33.8-10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.33.8-10","value":"Deut.33.8-10"}],"t":"ref","v":"33:8-10"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.17.7-9","r":"2Chr.17.7-9","rawR":"2Chr.17.7-9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.17.7-9","value":"2Chr.17.7-9"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 17:7-9"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ezek.44.23","r":"Ezek.44.23","rawR":"Ezek.44.23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezek.44.23","value":"Ezek.44.23"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ez 44:23"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Mic.3.11","r":"Mic.3.11","rawR":"Mic.3.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mic.3.11","value":"Mic.3.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mi 3:11"},"). God himself was thought of as a teacher (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.25.8,12","r":"Ps.25.8,12","rawR":"Ps.25.8,12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.25.8,12","value":"Ps.25.8,12"}],"t":"ref","v":"Pss 25:8, 12"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.27.11","r":"Ps.27.11","rawR":"Ps.27.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.27.11","value":"Ps.27.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"27:11"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.32.8","r":"Ps.32.8","rawR":"Ps.32.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.32.8","value":"Ps.32.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"32:8"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.86.11","r":"Ps.86.11","rawR":"Ps.86.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.86.11","value":"Ps.86.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"86:11"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.2.3","r":"Isa.2.3","rawR":"Isa.2.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.2.3","value":"Isa.2.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 2:3"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["In the NT the Greek noun for “teacher” and the verb “to teach” are widely used. John the Baptist was called a teacher (",{"href":"?bref=Luke.3.12","r":"Luke.3.12","rawR":"Luke.3.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.3.12","value":"Luke.3.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lk 3:12"},"). The term is used more than 30 times of Jesus (",{"href":"?bref=Matt.4.23","r":"Matt.4.23","rawR":"Matt.4.23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.4.23","value":"Matt.4.23"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mt 4:23"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Matt.5.2","r":"Matt.5.2","rawR":"Matt.5.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.5.2","value":"Matt.5.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"5:2"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Matt.7.29","r":"Matt.7.29","rawR":"Matt.7.29","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.7.29","value":"Matt.7.29"}],"t":"ref","v":"7:29"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Matt.9.35","r":"Matt.9.35","rawR":"Matt.9.35","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.9.35","value":"Matt.9.35"}],"t":"ref","v":"9:35"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Matt.11.1","r":"Matt.11.1","rawR":"Matt.11.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.11.1","value":"Matt.11.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"11:1"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Mark.1.21","r":"Mark.1.21","rawR":"Mark.1.21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mark.1.21","value":"Mark.1.21"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mk 1:21"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Mark.2.13","r":"Mark.2.13","rawR":"Mark.2.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mark.2.13","value":"Mark.2.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"2:13"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Mark.4.1-2","r":"Mark.4.1-2","rawR":"Mark.4.1-2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mark.4.1-2","value":"Mark.4.1-2"}],"t":"ref","v":"4:1-2"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Mark.6.2,6,34","r":"Mark.6.2,6,34","rawR":"Mark.6.2,6,34","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mark.6.2,6,34","value":"Mark.6.2,6,34"}],"t":"ref","v":"6:2, 6, 34"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Luke.4.15,31","r":"Luke.4.15,31","rawR":"Luke.4.15,31","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.4.15,31","value":"Luke.4.15,31"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lk 4:15, 31"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Luke.5.3","r":"Luke.5.3","rawR":"Luke.5.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.5.3","value":"Luke.5.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"5:3"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Luke.6.6","r":"Luke.6.6","rawR":"Luke.6.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.6.6","value":"Luke.6.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"6:6"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=John.6.59","r":"John.6.59","rawR":"John.6.59","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.6.59","value":"John.6.59"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jn 6:59"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=John.7.14,28","r":"John.7.14,28","rawR":"John.7.14,28","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.7.14,28","value":"John.7.14,28"}],"t":"ref","v":"7:14, 28"},"; etc.). People recognized his teaching as authoritative (",{"href":"?bref=Matt.7.29","r":"Matt.7.29","rawR":"Matt.7.29","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.7.29","value":"Matt.7.29"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mt 7:29"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Mark.1.22","r":"Mark.1.22","rawR":"Mark.1.22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mark.1.22","value":"Mark.1.22"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mk 1:22"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Luke.4.32","r":"Luke.4.32","rawR":"Luke.4.32","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.4.32","value":"Luke.4.32"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lk 4:32"},"). Even as a boy of 12 he conversed in a profound way with the teachers of the law in the temple (",{"href":"?bref=Luke.2.46","r":"Luke.2.46","rawR":"Luke.2.46","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.2.46","value":"Luke.2.46"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lk 2:46"},"). These men were often associated with the Pharisees (",{"href":"?bref=Luke.5.17","r":"Luke.5.17","rawR":"Luke.5.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.5.17","value":"Luke.5.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"5:17"},"). Gamaliel was a Pharisee and a teacher of the law (",{"href":"?bref=Acts.5.34","r":"Acts.5.34","rawR":"Acts.5.34","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Acts.5.34","value":"Acts.5.34"}],"t":"ref","v":"Acts 5:34"},"). The term “rabbi” was often used to denote teacher. The rabbi was held in great honor. In the early church the teacher was widely recognized (",{"href":"?bref=Acts.13.1","r":"Acts.13.1","rawR":"Acts.13.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Acts.13.1","value":"Acts.13.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Acts 13:1"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Cor.12.28-29","r":"1Cor.12.28-29","rawR":"1Cor.12.28-29","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Cor.12.28-29","value":"1Cor.12.28-29"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Cor 12:28-29"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Eph.4.11","r":"Eph.4.11","rawR":"Eph.4.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Eph.4.11","value":"Eph.4.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Eph 4:11"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Tim.1.11","r":"2Tim.1.11","rawR":"2Tim.1.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Tim.1.11","value":"2Tim.1.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Tm 1:11"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Jas.3.1","r":"Jas.3.1","rawR":"Jas.3.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jas.3.1","value":"Jas.3.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jas 3:1"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Teacher","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Dt 6:7, 20-25","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.6.7,20-25","rawQueryValue":"Deut.6.7,20-25","sourceRefExact":"Deut.6.7,20-25"},{"anchorText":"11:19-21","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.11.19-21","rawQueryValue":"Deut.11.19-21","sourceRefExact":"Deut.11.19-21"},{"anchorText":"Lv 10:11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Lev.10.11","rawQueryValue":"Lev.10.11","sourceRefExact":"Lev.10.11"},{"anchorText":"Dt 24:8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.24.8","rawQueryValue":"Deut.24.8","sourceRefExact":"Deut.24.8"},{"anchorText":"33:8-10","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.33.8-10","rawQueryValue":"Deut.33.8-10","sourceRefExact":"Deut.33.8-10"},{"anchorText":"2 Chr 17:7-9","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workst